        "number": 1,
        "title": "An evening in Soweto",
        "narrative": "When the lights went out, a girl imagined a little glow above her hand. It was a storybook power, not something people can do in real life.",
        "illustrationDescription": "A girl at a kitchen table during an evening power interruption; an adult nearby; a clearly imaginary glow.",
        "characterRefs": [
          "girl"
        ],
        "learningMoment": "Electricity powers many useful things. Magical powers belong to fiction.",
        "translation": {
          "text": "Ha mabone a tima, ngoanana o ile a inahanela khanya e nyenyane ka holim'a letsoho la hae. E ne e le matla a bukeng ea lipale, eseng ntho eo batho ba ka e etsang bophelong ba sebele.",
