      {
        "number": 2,
        "title": "A question for tomorrow",
        "narrative": "At school, she asked how a light could shine. Her teacher brought a small classroom battery kit. No one touched a wall socket or loose wire.",
        "illustrationDescription": "Teacher demonstrating a purpose-made enclosed battery learning kit to children.",
        "characterRefs": [
          "girl"
        ],
        "learningMoment": "Ask an adult to help with science activities. Never experiment with mains electricity.",
        "translation": {
          "text": "Sekolong, o ile a botsa hore na lebone le ka khanya joang. Tichere ea hae e ile ea tlisa sete e nyenyane ea libeteri ea tlelaseng. Ha ho motho ea ileng a ama sokete ea leboteng kapa terata e hlephileng.",
